  "text": "The loop checks out: the 0s and 6s frames are identical. I've finished the background and I'm done checking it.\n\n**What's in the comp**\n- **Blobs:** four soft orbs, named *Blob Purple*, *Blob Teal*, *Blob Violet* and *Blob Cyan*. Each is a stack of concentric low-opacity circles, which fakes a blur. They drift in slow ellipses, and the two smaller ones also breathe slightly in scale.\n- **Dot grid:** a 16×9 grid of small dots, built as 9 row layers named *Dots Row 1–9*. Each row pulses in opacity between about 8% and 52%. The rows are phase-shifted, so a soft wave ripples down the screen.\n- **Background:** solid `#0b0720`.\n\n**Why it loops:** every motion is a sine or cosine with exactly one cycle per 6 seconds, driven by expressions rather than keyframes. Nothing eases to a stop or jumps at the seam. The 6.0s frame sits just past the end of the comp, so playback goes from 5.97s straight back to 0s.\n\n**Limits and tweaks**\n- The editor has no blur effect, so the soft edges are an approximation. At 100% they look gently banded, and a blur or gradient pass in your final output would smooth them.\n- If you want it calmer, reduce the drift amplitudes (80–140px now) or the dot pulse range.",
